  "unresolvedAiThreads": [
    {
      "threadId": "PRRT_kwDORKRjBc6eDdoT",
      "replyToCommentDatabaseId": 3902896722,
      "path": "VAA.EAPI.Microservices/VAA.EAPI.Infrastructure.Email/Repository/CcpRepository.cs",
      "line": 33,
      "url": "https://github.com/VAAD1ST/eapi/pull/1731#discussion_r3902896722",
      "author": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer",
      "body": "`SendEmail` accepts a non-null `SendEmailRequest`, but the new guard uses `request?.To` without actually handling `request == null` (it would still throw later in `MapRequest`). This null-conditional is misleading; fail fast for null requests and pass `request.To` explicitly to the suppression policy.",
      "decision": "valid",
      "resolutionComment": "Added an explicit ArgumentNullException guard at the start of CcpRepository.SendEmail and passed request.To directly to EmailRecipientPolicy. Added regression coverage confirming a null request fails fast with the request parameter name."
    },
    {
      "threadId": "PRRT_kwDORKRjBc6eDdpW",
      "replyToCommentDatabaseId": 3902896820,
      "path": "VAA.EAPI.Microservices/VAA.EAPI.Infrastructure.Email/Policies/EmailRecipientPolicy.cs",
      "line": 46,
      "url": "https://github.com/VAAD1ST/eapi/pull/1731#discussion_r3902896820",
      "author": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer",
      "body": "`ShouldSuppressAcmRequest` only searches `Descendants()`, so it will miss `<rtEvent ... />` when it is the document root. Using `DescendantsAndSelf()` makes suppression robust regardless of whether `rtEvent` is nested in a SOAP envelope or is the root element.",
      "decision": "valid",
      "resolutionComment": "Updated ShouldSuppressAcmRequest to search document.Root.DescendantsAndSelf(), so rtEvent is detected both as the XML root and when nested in an envelope. Added regression coverage for a root rtEvent targeting the under-18 dummy domain."
    }
  ],
